```
function largestPrimeFactor(num) {
  let largest = 0;
  for (let i = 2; i <= num; i++) {
    while (num % i === 0) {
      largest = i;
      num /= i;
    }
  }
  return largest;
}
function factorial(num) {
  let result = 1;
  for (let i = 2; i <= num; i++) {
    result *= i;
  }
  return result;
}
```
The `largestPrimeFactor(num)` function uses a while loop to continuously divide the number by the smallest possible factor until it can no longer be divided. It then returns the largest factor that was used in the division.
The `factorial(num)` function uses a for loop to multiply each integer from 2 to the input number together, resulting in the factorial of the input number.
