One of the most significant secrets uncovered through espionage during World War I was the Zimmerman Telegram. This was a message sent by the German Foreign Secretary Arthur Zimmerman to the German ambassador in Mexico, proposing that Mexico should declare war on the United States in exchange for German support in regaining territory lost to the US in the Mexican-American War. The interception and decoding of this message by British intelligence was a major factor in the US decision to enter the war on the side of the Allies.
