Here's an example of how to generate a summary of the article using PHP-ML:
<?php
    require_once 'vendor/autoload.php';
    use NlpTools\Tokenizers\WhitespaceTokenizer;
    use NlpTools\Utils\StopWords;
    use NlpTools\Stemmers\PorterStemmer;
    use NlpTools\Similarity\CosineSimilarity;

    $servername = "localhost";
    $username = "username";
    $password = "password";
    $dbname = "database_name";
    // Create connection
    $conn = new mysqli($servername, $username, $password, $dbname);
    // Check connection
    if ($conn->connect_error) {
        die("Connection failed: " . $conn->connect_error);
    }
    // Retrieve latest news article
    $sql = "SELECT * FROM news_articles ORDER BY date_published DESC LIMIT 1";
    $result = $conn->query($sql);
    if ($result->num_rows > 0) {
        // Output data of the latest article
        while($row = $result->fetch_assoc()) {
            echo "<h2>" . $row["title"] . "</h2>";
            echo "<p>" . $row["content"] . "</p>";
            // Generate summary
            $tokenizer = new WhitespaceTokenizer();
            $stemmer = new PorterStemmer();
            $stopwords = new StopWords();
            $similarity = new CosineSimilarity();
            $summary = "";
            $sentences = preg_split('/(?<=[.?!])\s+(?=[a-z])/i', $row["content"]);
            $keywords = array();
            foreach ($sentences as $sentence) {
                $tokens = $tokenizer->tokenize($sentence);
                $tokens = array_filter($tokens, function($token) use ($stopwords) {
                    return !$stopwords->isStopWord($token);
                });
                $tokens = array_map(function($token) use ($stemmer) {
                    return $stemmer->stem($token);
                }, $tokens);
                $keywords[] = $tokens;
            }
            $query = $keywords[count($keywords) - 1];
            for ($i = 0; $i < count($keywords) - 1; $i++) {
                $sim = $similarity->similarity($query, $keywords[$i]);
                if ($sim > 0.5) {
                    $summary .= $sentences[$i] . " ";
                }
            }
            echo "<p><strong>Summary:</strong> " . $summary . "</p>";
        }
    } else {
        echo "0 results";
    }
    $conn->close();
?>
This code uses the Porter stemmer to normalize the words, removes stop words, and calculates the cosine similarity between the query (last sentence of the article) and each sentence in the article. If the similarity is above a certain threshold (0.5 in this case), the sentence is included in the summary. The summary is then displayed below the article.

