To generate a list of three character names for a fictional work that conforms to the given specifications, we can use a combination of HTML and JavaScript. Here is the complete code:
```
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
	<title>Three Character Names with Phonetic Alphabet</title>
	<script>
		function generateNames() {
			var phoneticAlphabet = ["Alpha", "Bravo", "Charlie", "Delta", "Echo", "Foxtrot", "Golf", "Hotel", "India", "Juliet", "Kilo", "Lima", "Mike", "November", "Oscar", "Papa", "Quebec", "Romeo", "Sierra", "Tango", "Uniform", "Victor", "Whiskey", "Xray", "Yankee", "Zulu"];
			var names = [];
			while (names.length < 3) {
				var name = "";
				for (var i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
					var letter = phoneticAlphabet[Math.floor(Math.random() * phoneticAlphabet.length)];
					name += letter.charAt(Math.floor(Math.random() * letter.length));
				}
				names.push(name);
			}
			document.getElementById("names").innerHTML = names.join(", ");
		}
	</script>
</head>
<body>
	<h1>Three Character Names with Phonetic Alphabet</h1>
	<p>Click the button to generate a list of three character names that contain at least one letter from the phonetic alphabet:</p>
	<button onclick="generateNames()">Generate Names</button>
	<p id="names"></p>
</body>
</html>
```
Here's how this code works:
1. We define an array called `phoneticAlphabet` that contains all the letters of the phonetic alphabet.
2. We define a function called `generateNames()` that will generate three random names that conform to the given specifications.
3. Inside the `generateNames()` function, we create an empty array called `names` to hold the generated names.
4. We use a `while` loop to generate three names. The loop will continue until the `names` array has three elements.
5. Inside the loop, we create an empty string called `name` to hold the generated name.
